<div>&nbsp;</div>
</div>
<div>
<div dir=3D"auto">Hi, Franki.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">I have a predicament.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">On one hand, I want to establish a reliable relationship =
with you. I want you to know I'm dependable and you can count on me. This i=
s really important to me.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">On the other hand, I really need to go home to Kentucky a=
t some point. It is very likely the last time I will ever see my mother. Th=
is is really important to me too.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">I was going to go this summer, but I couldn't turn down t=
he Humbug position. Not only is it my favorite place on earth (literally), =
I get to experience it with the bustling summer activity of the coast!</div=
>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">And I was looking forward to the same kind of experience =
at Tugman in September, when the park is likely quite busy and active and I=
'd be responsible for greeting new visitors as relief host.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">I really can't tell you how much it meant to me you exten=
ded the offer to me and I want more than anything to do it. But I have a pr=
oblem...</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">I started making plans to go home this winter and remembe=
red why I came to Oregon in the first place: winters are harsh in Kentucky =
and the parks are closed. I literally can't travel there then.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">After Umpqua in April, I spend two months at Humbug. I'd =
like to go home after that. But this means backing out of my September assi=
gnment at Tugman.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">I know that you would accept this. But I need more than t=
hat from you. I need to know you understand how torn I feel about it and th=
at it's not a reflection of my future reliability or passion for working wi=
th you at your parks. And I need to
 know this won't hurt me - as you know I already backed out of the very dum=
b decision to go to a day use area away from the coast, and I have no idea =
how that information appears in your systems.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">I'm trying to build a new life here, but my old life has =
some loose ends I need to confront. Can you help me?</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">Sam</div>
